WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.460
BRIAN RICE: Hi, everybody.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.120
I hope you're enjoying
Google Cloud Next so far.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.040
In this session, we're
going to talk to you

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.180
about the value of
getting a Google Cloud

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.330
certification to help
you in your career

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.180
and to help advance the
projects that you're

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.120
involved in in the world
of cloud computing.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.510
My name is Brian Rice, and
I work on Google's Cloud's

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.190
Learning Portfolio Team.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.668
And I'm joined today
by my colleague, Osaze.

00:00:38.668 --> 00:00:39.960
OSAZE IMASUEN: Hello, everyone.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.750
My name is Osaze Imasuen.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.460
And I'm a technical
program manager

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.320
in Google Global Networking.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.540
Really excited to be here and
looking forward to this talk.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.100
BRIAN RICE: Thank you so much.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.090
Here's the way we're going to
structure our session today.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.150
I'm going to kick it off
by talking about the roles

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.920
that are out there
in the world of cloud

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.790
computing and their demand and
how that's shaping and changing

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:07.060
as we move further and
further into the cloud era.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.210
I'm going to talk about
the learning resources

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.520
that Google Cloud
makes available to help

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.840
people achieve a wide range of
Google Cloud certifications.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.460
Then I'm going to
bring on Osaze.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.970
And he's going to tell us
about how certifications helped

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.470
him propel his career path.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.680
Finally, we'll wrap
it up by talking

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.160
about the benefits of
Google Cloud certifications,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.870
both to the people
who achieve them

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.990
and to the teams that
they're a part of.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.110
Let's start off by talking about
the demand for cloud computing

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.780
roles.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.630
We recently did a
survey where leaders

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:47.020
were asked about the barriers
that they had to cloud success.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.540
And over 80% of them identified
a skills gap on their team

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.580
as a top barrier.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.350
And this is a really
significant problem

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.300
if you think about the fact that
more than 90% of those leaders

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.570
expect to have increased use
of cloud over the next three

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:04.480
years.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.060
This tells us that skills are
a critical factor in companies'

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.520
move to the cloud.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.030
And we know it's of growing
importance to the cloud

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:19.230
community, because job
postings that were specifically

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.370
calling for cloud skills
grew by more than 40%

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:27.720
over the two years that ended
in the first quarter of 2021.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.670
And of course, there
was a lot of change

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.670
and a lot of upheaval
over that period.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.940
This significant growth
tells us about the fact

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:40.410
that skills are fuel for
companies moving into the cloud

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:44.590
and revolutionizing
the way they work.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.380
We at Google Cloud are
especially proud of the fact

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.500
that, in a survey conducted
by Global Knowledge,

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.480
the top two paying IT
certifications in the year 2021

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.500
in the US were both Google
Cloud certifications.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.910
We take this both as testimonial
to the value of Google Cloud

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:06.790
itself and also to
the programs that we

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.000
offer for recognizing
people's skills

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.430
and helping people train
themselves up so that they

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:16.380
can achieve those credentials.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:21.260
Now, cloud computing
always requires an approach

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:26.600
to learning and credentialing
that is focused on job roles.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.750
After all, the roles
that people play

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.740
is how people get value
out of cloud computing.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:39.590
Google Cloud technology training
is aimed at cloud solutions

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:43.220
rather than following
particular products boundaries.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:47.330
And it's key to the solutions
that customers tried to pursue,

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.890
which was their
reason for getting

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.600
into the cloud in
the first place.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.920
Now I'd like to talk with you
about the resources that we

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.260
make available to
help people skill up

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:02.040
and the certifications that
we make available to recognize

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.810
people's skill levels.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:09.180
Now, when you're leading
a team of professionals,

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.640
you have to keep in
mind that people are all

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.380
starting in different places.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.410
Everybody on a team
starts with a wide variety

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.779
of existing skill levels.

00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:22.680
Also, people have different
preferred learning styles.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.600
The same kind of
learning experience

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.310
doesn't work for everybody.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:31.440
So that's why we offer a wide
variety of choices for people

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.300
consuming our offerings.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.670
Some people prefer
to consume training

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.280
in a traditional
classroom-style format,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:42.060
either with a live instructor
or with virtual instructor-led

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:42.870
training.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:45.870
We have a worldwide network of
authorized training partners

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.730
that does just that.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.640
Other learners want the
increased convenience

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.460
and flexibility of
consuming online training

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.450
with virtual lectures
and online assessments.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.940
In order to help these
people, we make our training

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.460
available in online
channels as well,

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.510
with online training partners.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:09.960
Both of those two modes
contain the same hands-on labs,

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:15.120
in which people can gain real
world skills using real Google

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.660
Cloud, not a simulation, that
gives them the confidence

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.420
to do new things on the job.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:26.190
Finally, some learners want a
maximum amount of flexibility.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:29.490
They want a la carte
learning, snackable learning.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.180
That's why we also make
available a wide portfolio

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.800
of hands-on lab exercises that
can be consumed individually

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.600
in a safe sandbox environment.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.230
Now, all of these
lead up to achieving

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.200
professional and
associate-level certifications.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.640
These are benchmarks that a team
can adopt to bring everybody up

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.320
to a baseline of skill.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.870
That's how they know they
have the right foundation

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.360
for innovating and
for scaling up.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.130
Now, the benchmark concept
is very, very important

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.490
in the way we build
our certifications.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:13.180
Their content is defined
by subject matter experts.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.400
And they're key
to real-world job

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.560
roles and the uses to which
people put Google Cloud

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.670
technology.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:24.070
That's why Google
Cloud certifications

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.830
have significant benefit
not just to individuals,

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:28.630
but to companies as well.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:32.725
They're a well defined set
of skills that fuels growth.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.800
There's a wide variety
of certifications,

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.250
because we know that people
start at different points

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.960
and because we know
that people have

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.180
a wide variety of interests.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.510
The certifications range
from being targeted

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.120
at people with no
prior cloud skills

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:55.410
or experience all the way up
to people who have three years

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:59.310
or more of industry experience
and in a wide variety

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.050
of subject matter areas.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:06.310
Our certifications are organized
into three main categories.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.610
Two of these categories contain
certifications that are aimed

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.250
at hands-on technical
professionals--

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.980
the associate-level and
the professional-level

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.180
certifications.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.590
Here's the difference.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:21.040
Associate-level certifications,
such as Associate Cloud

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.960
Engineer, challenge the
candidate for the cert to map

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.920
from technical requirements
to the way a customer would

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.750
implement a solution.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.600
The professional level
of certifications

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.650
introduces one more layer,
challenging the candidate

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.260
to map from business
requirements,

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.770
through technical requirements,
to the details of the way

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.500
the customer
implementation would work.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.020
Finally, our credential
that is aimed

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:53.470
at anyone involved in
or impacted by the move

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.410
to the cloud, Cloud
Digital Leader,

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:00.520
contains three main bodies
of knowledge that it covers--

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.590
general cloud
knowledge, knowledge

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:05.350
of Google Cloud in
particular, and awareness

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:08.320
of the business value
and role of a variety

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.876
of important Google
Cloud Services.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.040
Let me give you more
information about the exams

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.620
that we make available.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.880
They're a two-hour experience.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:20.830
And they're offered
in a multiple choice

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.110
and multiple select format.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.540
The exams don't
have prerequisites

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:30.250
in that you are not required to
complete any specific training

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:33.250
or any specific
prior certifications

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.780
in order to attempt them.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:40.360
We do recommend that people
have hands-on experience

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:44.169
for our certifications that call
for that in their descriptions.

00:08:44.169 --> 00:08:48.460
And we also encourage people
to structure their preparation

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.980
and make sure they come
in with the knowledge

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.930
that each credential calls for.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:56.050
But no prerequisites
in the realm

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:59.740
of training or other
certifications are enforced.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.110
The exams are delivered
at your choice

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.840
of either a remote
location, in which case

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.750
the proctoring for the
exams is done online,

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:11.020
or you can go to a
physical testing center

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:15.900
and take an exam in an
on-site proctored system.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.150
Finally, we make available
official study guides,

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:23.000
in addition to all of
the other resources

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.990
that we make available.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:29.940
These books are available
from major resellers of books.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.940
At this point, I'd
like to bring Osaze on.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.820
Osaze, we wanted to
ask you to join us

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:39.900
today to tell us about
your career journey

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:42.540
through the lens
of certification.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:46.560
Could I ask you to start off
by telling us about your career

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.220
path before the cloud?

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.390
OSAZE IMASUEN: Sure, Brian.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:55.370
So my career has spanned
approximately two decades.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:59.450
And I've had a variety
of roles, from hands-on

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.620
to technical leadership, to
just pure leadership roles.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.950
And I would say
that certifications

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.340
and learning and relearning
has been a key component.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.350
It enabled me to
progress through

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:17.780
from being an engineer up
into leadership positions.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:20.060
Why do I say this?

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.330
Early on in my
career, I started out

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:26.720
trying to build
infrastructures for companies

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:29.480
and deliver their IT
solutions internally.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.240
But I found that the moment
I added certifications

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.000
and that learning
experience to my journey,

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.110
it accelerated, one, my
knowledge, my learning,

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.377
and then also my scope
of responsibility.

00:10:41.377 --> 00:10:43.460
So it's something that has
worked very well for me

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.330
in my career.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.890
And it's something
that I continue

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:51.170
to use and reuse over and over.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.400
BRIAN RICE: Super.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:54.950
And tell us more about
what happened when you

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.897
started moving into the cloud.

00:10:57.897 --> 00:10:58.730
OSAZE IMASUEN: Sure.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:03.230
So before the
journey to the cloud,

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:09.320
my organization would
procure, build, and operate

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:11.380
our own internal resources.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:13.580
So think of private cloud.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:18.950
And at some point, we realized
that the cost and also the time

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:24.140
to delivery made us not meet
certain business requirements.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:27.080
And we had to start looking
at the option of moving

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.850
some of those
workloads to the cloud.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:32.060
Now, we didn't migrate
everything over all in one day.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.430
We started out in a
step by step process

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:38.990
by doing the trial for setting
non-critical workloads first

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:42.530
to get a feel for how things
will operate in the cloud

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:46.160
and also what the security
framework would be,

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.780
because that is a
huge consideration

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:50.390
for anyone trying to make
that journey into the cloud.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.550
Over time, as a
team, we got more

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:55.160
confident in using
resources and understanding

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.570
the products in the cloud.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.140
We were able to move
even critical workloads

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:00.987
into the cloud.

00:12:00.987 --> 00:12:02.570
And one of the
benefits, which I think

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.520
is perhaps well-known
in the industry,

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:08.900
is, when you run your
own resources internally,

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:11.430
you most often plan
for peak demand.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.130
And that means that,
a lot of times,

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.650
you have resources
idling, not being used,

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:18.440
whereas in the cloud, in
the more pay-per-use model,

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:24.800
you're able to more effectively
use resources and also reduce

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:28.880
your spend if you plan
your resources properly.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:29.780
BRIAN RICE: Indeed.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:32.390
Well, to sum up,
can you tell us now

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:38.030
about how certifications played
a role in your own transition

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.767
to the cloud?

00:12:39.767 --> 00:12:40.600
OSAZE IMASUEN: Sure.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:45.520
So I've always enjoyed
learning and relearning.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:48.100
So for me,
certifications help me

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.100
focus my attention
over a period of time

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:54.850
to learn that new
technology or learn

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.470
whatever is new in that space.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:59.110
So an example with
Google Cloud is--

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:01.960
over a couple of years,
I was aware of using

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.480
Google Cloud platform and
also some other providers.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.840
But when I made that
conscious effort to say,

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:11.920
I'm going to get certified,
it helped focus and narrow

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:15.190
my learning to make sure
that I mastered the content

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.890
and understood the
products and offerings

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:20.170
and how they related
to my business.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:23.740
The end result is I've been
able to achieve certifications

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:27.670
in some of the
professional-level engineer

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.480
programs like the Professional
Cloud Architect, Data

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:34.780
Professional, and some of
the other professional-level

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:36.040
certifications.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:39.580
Why I find these
helpful is it helps

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:45.370
cover a range of topics that are
relevant to the business of IT

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:46.930
and computing today.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:52.090
And the certification
itself provides knowledge.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.200
That is for sure.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.910
It gives you the
confidence to be

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:58.870
able to interact with either
external or internal peers

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:01.520
or customers.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:06.520
It also gives you
that confidence.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.770
And, as well, there's
also the Google swag

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:10.668
in terms of the goodies,
the bags, and all

00:14:10.668 --> 00:14:12.460
the other nice things
that Google gives you

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:14.170
when you're certified.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.023
BRIAN RICE: So true.

00:14:15.023 --> 00:14:16.690
OSAZE IMASUEN: Thank
you so much, Osaze,

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:19.250
for telling us your story.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.680
Now, the last section
of our presentation

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:25.370
is focused on the benefits of
Google Cloud certifications,

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:30.660
both to individuals and to
companies and the ecosystem.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:33.660
We did a survey in
the beginning of 2020

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:37.770
of people who had achieved
Google Cloud certifications

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:41.640
using an independent
third-party organization.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:44.590
Of the people that
we surveyed, 78%

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:46.960
said that they had gotten
additional confidence

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:49.270
in their professional
future because they

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:52.120
got this certification.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:56.980
82% felt like they
now had a special way

00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:00.520
to prove their cloud
skill competency

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.680
to potential recruiters.

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:06.670
83% felt that their
resume or CV was now

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.520
more attractive to
prospective employers.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:14.380
And finally, 85% said that they
themselves felt more confident

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.920
in their cloud skills.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:20.350
IT leaders have also been
surveyed about the impact

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.880
of certification.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:26.560
Out of those who authorized
training for their teams

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:29.440
within the last 12 months
in a different survey,

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.560
2/3 did so specifically
with the aim

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:36.010
of preparing their team
members for certification

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:38.170
or re-certification.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:44.170
93% of those leaders agreed that
certified employees add value

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:47.950
to their organizations
well beyond the sheer cost

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:50.230
of the certification itself.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.100
How much was that?

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.730
Well, 63% of them were
comfortable estimating

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:58.180
that the economic benefit
of those certified employees

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.370
was more than
$10,000 USD a year,

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:03.790
which is a significant
increment for what

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:08.740
is comparatively a small
investment in skills

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.380
and knowledge.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:15.520
As Osaze mentioned, there's
a wide variety of benefits

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:16.870
for getting certification.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.000
And some of them are swag.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.070
Folks who achieve our
professional-level

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:24.820
certifications do get
excellent merchandise

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:28.330
that allows them to show off
their credentials in public.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.510
Everybody gets a
digital badge that they

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:35.080
can put on their
profiles on social media

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.170
and display in other ways.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:40.510
Professional-level
certified people

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:45.850
also get access to special
events at Google Cloud

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.500
Next and other venues.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.230
They get access to the Google
Cloud certified community

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:53.050
so that they can exchange
ideas and knowledge

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:56.590
with other certified people
and seek out networking

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:59.380
opportunities as well.

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:01.740
Now, this talk
wouldn't be complete

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:04.440
if we didn't have
something new to present.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:08.220
In order to help the
broad ecosystem get

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.680
more cloud and
Google Cloud skills,

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:14.099
today we are announcing
Google Cloud skills boost.

00:17:14.099 --> 00:17:17.730
It's a brand new way to
consume Google Cloud learning.

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:22.170
It makes more than 700
labs, courses, and tools

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:25.270
for preparing for our
certifications available.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.450
And for the next
month, we're making

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:30.030
it available to all of
our customers and partners

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:31.410
at no cost.

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:36.330
The URL is
g.co/cloud/freetraining.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.070
And we hope that
everybody listening

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.870
will take advantage
of this offer

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.780
and see what we are
making available to help

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:46.200
people take their careers
to the next level.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.270
At this point, I
want to thank Osaze

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:52.110
for joining us today and
telling us his story.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.650
And I'd like to thank everyone
in the audience for joining us.

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:59.200
And we wish you all the best
with your cloud careers.

